SWEET WLAN perf (patch 0273, sprint-wifi Part A 2026-11-09): (1) the keep poll thread is event-driven (100 us after a pass that handled items or with frames queued, 5 ms when idle, woken at once by en0_output through EN0_KICK) instead of a fixed 5 ms delay_for_interval; its alive line prints every 10 s with the rx/tx drop, tx-queue and batch counters; (2) data-path GAP lines (SWDP_GAP) print the 1st, 2nd, 4th ... occurrence of each text with its count (all counted, every one in the gap summary) instead of one printf per dropped frame; (3) the block accessors of struct swg_bus (sweet_wlan_g2.h rd_blk / wr_blk), used only by DP15 item/payload words in quiet (keep) mode: one cache pass per range instead of one per word; the batched store keeps every per-word check (engine: row kinds, old words vs shadows, read-back; glue: G2 + live L25 judge, link check before AND after the batch, swl25w_ok_blk = the per-word verdict for every word, swl25w_done per word). (4) every 5 s the keep thread reads the firmware RSSI (the read-only, judged WLC_GET_RSSI of swl25_live) and hands it to the kept Apple80211 link (sweet_wlan_a80211_kept_rssi, outside the en0 lock); review perf-c F1: the refresh runs only with ring 2 idle, never starts a DS round, and a soft stop inside it turns the refresh off with a GAP instead of ending the data path (a hard stop still ends it). (5) read-only timing counters (poll pass, link checks, judge, cache passes) printed per 10 s window. (6) perf-d: one link check per audited DP15 plan that ends in its doorbell (struct swg_bus plan): its host/DATA stores skip their own check, the doorbell keeps it (the argument of the batch: a link lost inside the plan fails it before its doorbell). No new hardware register, no new store kind, no new address: the same host/DATA words the per-word path stores.
